{"name":"UK ukspending/Contracts Finder awards for NovaSeq 6000 support plans running to 2029 (university and NHS genomic labs)","url":"https://ukspending.com/contracts/50927","access":"Open mirror, no login. Open contract 50927 (University of Birmingham: MiSeq, NextSeq 500, NextSeq 2000 and NovaSeq 6000 Silver Support Plans, 2025–2029). Then search ukspending.com for 'NovaSeq 6000', 'Silver Support', 'Gold Support' and 'NovaSeq X', and list buyer, value, start and end dates. Distinct from S751 (UKHSA reagent framework) and S859 (kit call-offs).","labels":["1A"],"rationale":"Multi-year 6000 support contracts signed in 2025 with end dates in 2029 give dated evidence that owners expect to run 6000s, and buy their reagents, past management's 'mostly done by end-2026'. That supports the long tail (management's 'permanent' view) but also bounds the pace of 1A conversion, so it can cut both ways. The useful output is the number and value of such contracts.","expected_payoff":"medium"},
